---
import {
  CheckCircle2,
  ExternalLink,
  FolderSync,
  Monitor,
  RefreshCw,
  Smartphone,
} from "@lucide/astro";

const syncthingUrl = "https://syncthing.net/";
---

<section
  id="cross-device-sync"
  class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface p-7 md:p-10"
>
  <div
    class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-vega-accent"
  >
    <FolderSync class="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" />
    Cross-Device Sync
  </div>

  <h2
    class="mt-4 font-headline text-[clamp(1.8rem,3.6vw,2.6rem)] font-black tracking-tight text-white"
  >
    Keep Vega in Sync Across Your Devices
  </h2>

  <p class="mt-3 max-w-[72ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-vega-muted">
    Vega synchronizes through your download folder. Share that folder between
    your devices to keep downloaded media, Continue Watching progress, and
    WatchList changes available across Vega Mobile and Desktop.
  </p>

  <article
    class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-vega-accent/30 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5"
  >
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
      <RefreshCw class="h-4 w-4 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
      <h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold">Recommended: Syncthing</h3>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted">
      Syncthing keeps a folder synchronized directly between your devices. It is
      open source and does not require uploading your Vega library to a central
      cloud storage provider.
    </p>
    <a
      class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-vega-accent px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-[#240900] transition hover:-translate-y-0.5"
      href={syncthingUrl}
      target="_blank"
      rel="noreferrer"
    >
      <ExternalLink class="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" />
      Visit Syncthing
    </a>
  </article>

  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <FolderSync class="h-4 w-4 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold">1. Share a Folder</h3>
      </div>
      <ol
        class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>Install Syncthing on every device you want to connect.</li>
        <li>Add the devices to each other using their Syncthing device IDs.</li>
        <li>Create a folder for Vega downloads on one device.</li>
        <li>Share that folder with your other devices and accept it there.</li>
        <li>Wait until Syncthing reports that the folder is up to date.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <CheckCircle2 class="h-4 w-4 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold">2. Connect Vega</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted">
        Configure Vega on every device to use its local copy of the same
        Syncthing folder. Vega creates a hidden <code
          class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white">.vega-sync</code
        > directory inside it automatically.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted">
        Do not manually copy, rename, or edit files in <code
          class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white">.vega-sync</code
        >. Each device maintains its own manifest there.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <Monitor class="h-4 w-4 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold">Desktop</h3>
      </div>
      <ol
        class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>Open <strong class="text-white">Settings</strong> in Vega.</li>
        <li>Find <strong class="text-white">Download Directory</strong>.</li>
        <li>Select the local Syncthing folder used for your Vega downloads.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <Smartphone class="h-4 w-4 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold">Android</h3>
      </div>
      <ol
        class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>Open <strong class="text-white">Settings</strong> in Vega.</li>
        <li>
          Under Downloads, open <strong class="text-white"
            >Download Location</strong
          >.
        </li>
        <li>Select the local folder managed by Syncthing.</li>
        <li>Allow folder access when Android asks for permission.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>
  </div>

  <article class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-5">
    <h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold text-white">
      Using Sync Day to Day
    </h3>
    <ul
      class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
    >
      <li>
        Keep Syncthing running on both devices until the folder is up to date.
      </li>
      <li>
        Open or return to Vega after Syncthing finishes transferring changes.
      </li>
      <li>
        When switching devices during an episode, pause playback and allow a
        short time for progress to reach the other device.
      </li>
      <li>
        Avoid downloading or editing the same media on two offline devices at
        the same time, as Syncthing may create conflict copies.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </article>

  <div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted">
      <strong class="text-white">Sync delayed?</strong> Check that Syncthing says
      <strong class="text-white">Up to Date</strong> on both devices, confirm both
      Vega installations use the shared download folder, then reopen Vega.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
